# Mutation cases for the `<content expr>` of a `<final>`'s `<donedata>` that names
# one value, in a `datamodel="sce-static"` machine generated as Python
# (docs/SCE_ACCEPTED_SUBSET.md §2.15).
#
# Run with
# `scripts/mutate sce-build/tests/mutations/a_static_python_donedata_content_value_is_the_whole_event_data_python.cases`.
#
# The expression is Python the lowering wrote, read from the policy's own
# attributes when the state is entered, and the template only places it: the
# value is the done event's whole data as the JSON `to_json_literal` writes (`4`,
# `"tally"`). A value that cannot be computed — a checked multiplication that
# overflows — raises `AlgorithmFailure`, and it is the evaluation that failed (W3C
# SCXML 5.5): `error.execution` is raised and the empty string is the content's
# value.
#
# What is easy to get wrong and reads as success: the zero of a failed value is a
# done event that looks complete, and the text of a value in place of its JSON is
# a number that is right and a string that has lost its quotes. The scenarios
# `static_donedata_content_value`, `_text` and `_lost` tell them apart.
#
# Python compiles nothing and its generated machines are gitignored, so the
# template reaches the tests only through the regeneration declared below. It is a
# `mutation_runtime_targets` for the reason the other Python casefiles give: what
# shows a mutation arrived is that the file on disk differed while the tests ran.
#
# Anchors are literal slices of the source; an edit that moves one is reported
# INCONCLUSIVE with the anchor quoted, never as a pass.

mutation_pytest backends/python/tests integration/static_datamodel/test_static_scenarios.py
mutation_regen scripts/regen_static_datamodel_python.sh
mutation_runtime_targets tools/codegen/templates/python/entry_exit_actions.py.jinja2
mutation_oracles backends/python/tests/integration/static_datamodel/test_static_scenarios.py sce-build/tests/fixtures/static_datamodel/scenarios/static_donedata_content_value.json sce-build/tests/fixtures/static_datamodel/scenarios/static_donedata_content_text.json sce-build/tests/fixtures/static_datamodel/scenarios/static_donedata_content_lost.json sce-build/tests/fixtures/static_datamodel/static_donedata_content.scxml

# ── A value that cannot be computed is the empty string ────────────

mutation_case "a donedata content value that failed is the zero of its type, not the empty string" <<'PY'
edit("tools/codegen/templates/python/entry_exit_actions.py.jinja2",
     "                _done_data = '\"\"'\n{% else %}",
     "                _done_data = '0'\n{% else %}")
PY

# ── The value is the JSON it is ────────────────────────────────────

mutation_case "a donedata content value is the text of the value, not its JSON" <<'PY'
edit("tools/codegen/templates/python/entry_exit_actions.py.jinja2",
     "{% else %}\n            _done_data = ({{ state.donedata.native_content_value }}).to_json_literal()\n",
     "{% else %}\n            _done_data = ({{ state.donedata.native_content_value }}).to_wire_string()\n")
PY
